 Let's, let's go for a walk and do that.

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:44.310
 So the, the first four rows here are a varietal called Triple Crown.

00:23:44.540 --> 00:23:50.050
 And the blackberries divide themselves into two types, which are Floricanes.

00:23:50.120 --> 00:23:51.800
 And Primo Canes.

00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:52.100
 Okay.

00:23:52.470 --> 00:23:59.910
 And all that means is that this variety, the Floricanes varieties, they send up canes called bull canes.

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:03.170
 And those canes do not bear fruit the first year.

00:24:04.010 --> 00:24:05.670
 Next year, they bear fruit.

00:24:05.850 --> 00:24:09.610
 So they come up in the fall or the winter when everything dies back.

00:24:09.730 --> 00:24:13.510
 You go in and you find the canes that had fruit on them this year.

00:24:13.650 --> 00:24:17.750
 You cut them out and you take the canes that are left and you trellis them.

00:24:18.190 --> 00:24:18.290
 Okay.

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:19.900
 It's a lot of work.

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:21.840
 Um, thank God for audio books.

