 And it, and it's black.

00:25:06.940 --> 00:25:11.010
 And there's black, and there's shiny black, and there's dull black.

00:25:11.810 --> 00:25:18.630
 But the thing that you're really looking for is those little bumps of a, of a berry, a

00:25:18.630 --> 00:25:22.010
 raspberry or a blackberry are called druplets.

00:25:22.690 --> 00:25:26.300
 And if you're in intimate terms with blackberries, you can just say drupes.

00:25:26.600 --> 00:25:26.840
 Okay.

00:25:26.980 --> 00:25:31.780
 And you can see on this one berry, these druplets are expanded.

00:25:31.960 --> 00:25:32.540
 They're swollen.

00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:33.060
 Uh-huh.

00:25:33.210 --> 00:25:34.760
 They look like they're about to burst.

00:25:34.920 --> 00:25:35.100
 Right.

00:25:35.540 --> 00:25:38.070
 And these druplets, not so much.

00:25:38.170 --> 00:25:39.510
 They're tighter and smaller, right?

00:25:39.630 --> 00:25:39.830
 Yeah.

00:25:40.160 --> 00:25:47.080
 So, if you, if you just pick for a few minutes, and you taste what you're picking, and you,

00:25:47.280 --> 00:25:49.160
 and you, now that you have a name for things.

00:25:49.280 --> 00:25:54.370
 So, naming things to me is very important, because you, once you name them, you can, you

00:25:54.370 --> 00:25:56.510
 can manipulate them as ideas in your head.

00:25:56.670 --> 00:25:56.770
 Right.

